{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"ced0611b616fd563505b4bc6","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui%40gmail.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"subject":"[PATCH 0/3] Handle optional IRQs correctly","messages":{"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com":{"id":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Kamal Dasu","address":"kamal.dasu@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Broadcom internal kernel review list","address":"bcm-kernel-feedback-list@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Florian Fainelli","address":"florian.fainelli@broadcom.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"bui duc phuc","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-13T08:52:10.000Z","iso":"2026-08-13T08:52:10.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH 0/3] Handle optional IRQs correctly","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"code","text":"From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi all,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The changes were found through code inspection while reviewing optional\nIRQ handling in I2C drivers."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I noticed that some drivers already handle the return value of\nplatform_get_irq_optional() explicitly, including i2c-designware-platdrv,\ni2c-ocores, and i2c-sh_mobile."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This series updates the affected drivers to properly handle errors from\nplatform_get_irq_optional() and distinguish a missing optional IRQ from\nother errors."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The series also fixes the handling of IRQ 0 in the brcmstb driver, since\n0 is not a valid IRQ number returned by platform_get_irq_optional()."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The series was only compile-tested."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,\nPhuc"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"bui duc phuc (3):\n  i2c: pca-platform: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup\n  i2c: brcmstb: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup\n  i2c: brcmstb: Correct optional IRQ handling"},{"kind":"code","text":" drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c      | 6 ++++--"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":" drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c | 5 ++++-\n 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)"},{"kind":"signature","text":"2.43.0","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com":{"id":"20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","references":["20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Kamal Dasu","address":"kamal.dasu@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Broadcom internal kernel review list","address":"bcm-kernel-feedback-list@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Florian Fainelli","address":"florian.fainelli@broadcom.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"bui duc phuc","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-13T08:52:11.000Z","iso":"2026-08-13T08:52:11.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH 1/3] i2c: pca-platform: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"code","text":"From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"platform_get_irq_optional() returns a positive IRQ number on success or\na negative error code on failure. For an optional IRQ, -ENXIO indicates\nthat no optional IRQ is available. Other errors, such as -EPROBE_DEFER\nand -EINVAL, should be propagated so that the caller can handle them\nappropriately."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Propagate negative errors other than -ENXIO."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:1:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:1:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","parentId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com":{"id":"20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","references":["20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Kamal Dasu","address":"kamal.dasu@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Broadcom internal kernel review list","address":"bcm-kernel-feedback-list@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Florian Fainelli","address":"florian.fainelli@broadcom.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"bui duc phuc","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-13T08:52:12.000Z","iso":"2026-08-13T08:52:12.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH 2/3] i2c: brcmstb: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"code","text":"From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"platform_get_irq_optional() returns a positive IRQ number on success or\na negative error code on failure. For an optional IRQ, -ENXIO indicates\nthat no optional IRQ is available. Other errors, such as -EPROBE_DEFER\nand -EINVAL, should be propagated so that the caller can handle them\nappropriately."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Propagate negative errors other than -ENXIO."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:2:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:2:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","parentId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com":{"id":"20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","references":["20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Kamal Dasu","address":"kamal.dasu@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Broadcom internal kernel review list","address":"bcm-kernel-feedback-list@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Florian Fainelli","address":"florian.fainelli@broadcom.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"bui duc phuc","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-13T08:52:13.000Z","iso":"2026-08-13T08:52:13.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH 3/3] i2c: brcmstb: Correct optional IRQ handling","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"code","text":"From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"dev->irq is assigned from platform_get_irq_optional(), which returns a\nnon-zero interrupt number on success or a negative error number on\nfailure. Therefore, 0 is not a valid IRQ number."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Check for a positive IRQ number before requesting the IRQ instead of\ntreating 0 as a valid IRQ."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Also use a positive IRQ number when reporting the operating mode. The\ndriver sets dev->irq to -1 when devm_request_irq() fails, so the mode\ncheck should only consider positive IRQ numbers as interrupt mode."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:3:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:3:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":3,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","parentId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"childrenByParent":{"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com":["20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"]},"chronologicalIds":["20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"patchSeries":[{"id":"1:handle optional irqs correctly","version":1,"total":3,"subjectStem":"Handle optional IRQs correctly","coverMessageId":"20260813085213.44001-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","members":[{"index":1,"messageId":"20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:1:0"},{"index":2,"messageId":"20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:2:0"},{"index":3,"messageId":"20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","patchId":"patch:20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:3:0"}],"incomplete":false}],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{"patch:20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:1:0":{"id":"patch:20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:1:0","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","subject":"[PATCH 1/3] i2c: pca-platform: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup","commitMessage":[],"files":[{"oldPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c","newPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c","displayPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c","status":"modified","hunks":[{"header":"@@ -139,8 +139,11 @@ static int i2c_pca_pf_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)","oldStart":139,"oldCount":8,"newStart":139,"newCount":11,"lines":[{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":139,"newLine":139},{"kind":"context","text":"\tirq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);","oldLine":140,"newLine":140},{"kind":"context","text":"\t/* If irq is 0, we do polling. */","oldLine":141,"newLine":141},{"kind":"deletion","text":"\tif (irq < 0)","oldLine":142},{"kind":"addition","text":"\tif (irq < 0) {","newLine":142},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t\tif (irq != -ENXIO)","newLine":143},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t\t\treturn irq;","newLine":144},{"kind":"context","text":"\t\tirq = 0;","oldLine":143,"newLine":145},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t}","newLine":146},{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":144,"newLine":147},{"kind":"context","text":"\ti2c = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*i2c), GFP_KERNEL);","oldLine":145,"newLine":148},{"kind":"context","text":"\tif (!i2c)","oldLine":146,"newLine":149},{"kind":"deletion","text":"- ","oldLine":147},{"kind":"metadata","text":"2.43.0"},{"kind":"metadata","text":""},{"kind":"metadata","text":""}]}],"binary":false}],"trailers":[],"rawText":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c\nindex c0f35ebbe37d..63c8ca1f1870 100644\n--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c\n+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pca-platform.c\n@@ -139,8 +139,11 @@ static int i2c_pca_pf_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)\n \n \tirq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);\n \t/* If irq is 0, we do polling. */\n-\tif (irq < 0)\n+\tif (irq < 0) {\n+\t\tif (irq != -ENXIO)\n+\t\t\treturn irq;\n \t\tirq = 0;\n+\t}\n \n \ti2c = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*i2c), GFP_KERNEL);\n \tif (!i2c)\n-- \n2.43.0\n\n","statistics":{"files":1,"additions":4,"deletions":2},"diagnostics":[]},"patch:20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:2:0":{"id":"patch:20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:2:0","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-3-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","subject":"[PATCH 2/3] i2c: brcmstb: Handle errors from optional IRQ lookup","commitMessage":[],"files":[{"oldPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","newPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","displayPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","status":"modified","hunks":[{"header":"@@ -648,6 +648,8 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)","oldStart":648,"oldCount":6,"newStart":648,"newCount":8,"lines":[{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":648,"newLine":648},{"kind":"context","text":"\t/* Get the interrupt number */","oldLine":649,"newLine":649},{"kind":"context","text":"\tdev->irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);","oldLine":650,"newLine":650},{"kind":"addition","text":"\tif (dev->irq < 0 && dev->irq != -ENXIO)","newLine":651},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t\treturn dev->irq;","newLine":652},{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":651,"newLine":653},{"kind":"context","text":"\t/* disable the bsc interrupt line */","oldLine":652,"newLine":654},{"kind":"context","text":"\tbrcmstb_i2c_enable_disable_irq(dev, INT_DISABLE);","oldLine":653,"newLine":655},{"kind":"deletion","text":"- ","oldLine":654},{"kind":"metadata","text":"2.43.0"},{"kind":"metadata","text":""},{"kind":"metadata","text":""}]}],"binary":false}],"trailers":[],"rawText":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\nindex 5fa30e8926c5..91525a36e575 100644\n--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\n+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\n@@ -648,6 +648,8 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)\n \n \t/* Get the interrupt number */\n \tdev->irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);\n+\tif (dev->irq < 0 && dev->irq != -ENXIO)\n+\t\treturn dev->irq;\n \n \t/* disable the bsc interrupt line */\n \tbrcmstb_i2c_enable_disable_irq(dev, INT_DISABLE);\n-- \n2.43.0\n\n","statistics":{"files":1,"additions":2,"deletions":1},"diagnostics":[]},"patch:20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:3:0":{"id":"patch:20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com:3:0","messageId":"20260813085213.44001-4-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","subject":"[PATCH 3/3] i2c: brcmstb: Correct optional IRQ handling","commitMessage":[],"files":[{"oldPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","newPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","displayPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c","status":"modified","hunks":[{"header":"@@ -655,7 +655,7 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)","oldStart":655,"oldCount":7,"newStart":655,"newCount":7,"lines":[{"kind":"context","text":"\tbrcmstb_i2c_enable_disable_irq(dev, INT_DISABLE);","oldLine":655,"newLine":655},{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":656,"newLine":656},{"kind":"context","text":"\t/* register the ISR handler */","oldLine":657,"newLine":657},{"kind":"deletion","text":"\tif (dev->irq >= 0) {","oldLine":658},{"kind":"addition","text":"\tif (dev->irq > 0) {","newLine":658},{"kind":"context","text":"\t\trc = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, dev->irq, brcmstb_i2c_isr,","oldLine":659,"newLine":659},{"kind":"context","text":"\t\t\t\t      IRQF_SHARED,","oldLine":660,"newLine":660},{"kind":"context","text":"\t\t\t\t      int_name ? int_name : pdev->name,","oldLine":661,"newLine":661}]},{"header":"@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)","oldStart":697,"oldCount":7,"newStart":697,"newCount":7,"lines":[{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":697,"newLine":697},{"kind":"context","text":"\tdev_info(dev->device, \"%s@%dhz registered in %s mode\\n\",","oldLine":698,"newLine":698},{"kind":"context","text":"\t\t int_name ? int_name : \" \", dev->clk_freq_hz,","oldLine":699,"newLine":699},{"kind":"deletion","text":"\t\t (dev->irq >= 0) ? \"interrupt\" : \"polling\");","oldLine":700},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t\t (dev->irq > 0) ? \"interrupt\" : \"polling\");","newLine":700},{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":701,"newLine":701},{"kind":"context","text":"\treturn 0;","oldLine":702,"newLine":702},{"kind":"context","text":"}","oldLine":703,"newLine":703},{"kind":"deletion","text":"- ","oldLine":704},{"kind":"metadata","text":"2.43.0"},{"kind":"metadata","text":""},{"kind":"metadata","text":""}]}],"binary":false}],"trailers":[],"rawText":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\nindex 91525a36e575..3adc73f3d608 100644\n--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\n+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-brcmstb.c\n@@ -655,7 +655,7 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)\n \tbrcmstb_i2c_enable_disable_irq(dev, INT_DISABLE);\n \n \t/* register the ISR handler */\n-\tif (dev->irq >= 0) {\n+\tif (dev->irq > 0) {\n \t\trc = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, dev->irq, brcmstb_i2c_isr,\n \t\t\t\t      IRQF_SHARED,\n \t\t\t\t      int_name ? int_name : pdev->name,\n@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ static int brcmstb_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)\n \n \tdev_info(dev->device, \"%s@%dhz registered in %s mode\\n\",\n \t\t int_name ? int_name : \" \", dev->clk_freq_hz,\n-\t\t (dev->irq >= 0) ? \"interrupt\" : \"polling\");\n+\t\t (dev->irq > 0) ? \"interrupt\" : \"polling\");\n \n \treturn 0;\n }\n-- \n2.43.0\n\n","statistics":{"files":1,"additions":2,"deletions":3},"diagnostics":[]}}}}